          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We find the reciprocal of the base <span class=\"math\">[MATH: ({\\color{blue}{2}}),]</span> and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the <em>opposite</em> sign <span class=\"math\">[MATH: ({{\\color{red}{+3}}}),]</span> as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2^{\u2212 3}|= ((1)/(2))^{3}; = ((1)/(2)) \u00d7 ((1)/(2)) \u00d7 ((1)/(2)); = ((1 \u00d7 1 \u00d7 1)/(2 \u00d7 2 \u00d7 2)); = (1)/(8)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We find the reciprocal of the base [MATH: ({\\color{blue}{2}}),] and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign [MATH: ({{\\color{red}{+3}}}),] as follows:\n\n[MATH: 2^{\u2212 3}|= ((1)/(2))^{3}; = ((1)/(2)) \u00d7 ((1)/(2)) \u00d7 ((1)/(2)); = ((1 \u00d7 1 \u00d7 1)/(2 \u00d7 2 \u00d7 2)); = (1)/(8)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
